            "meaning": "May Indra of great renown grant us well-being."
          }
        ],
        "chant": {
          "type": "Yajus",
          "delivery": "spoken",
          "intonation": "auspicious close",
          "usage": "Concluding blessing"
        }
      },
      {
        "chant_id": "YV-1-21",
        "source_yajurveda": "Vajasaneyi Samhita 1.21",
        "deity": "Agni",
        "theme": "Vow and truth",
        "verses": [
          {
            "verse_id": 1,
            "sanskrit": "अग्ने व्रतपते व्रतं चरिष्यामि तच्छकेयं तन्मे राध्यताम् । इदमहमनृतात्सत्यमुपैमि",
            "transliteration": "agne vratapate vrataṃ cariṣyāmi tac chakeyaṃ tan me rādhyatām | idam aham anṛtāt satyam upaimi",
            "meaning": "O Agni, Lord of vows, I shall observe the vow. May I be capable; may it succeed. From falsehood I pass to truth."
          }
        ],
        "chant": {
          "type": "Yajus",
          "delivery": "spoken",
          "intonation": "solemn ritual cadence",
          "usage": "Declaration of vow in Darśa–Pūrṇamāsa rite"
        }
      },
      {
        "chant_id": "YV-1-22",
        "source_yajurveda": "Vajasaneyi Samhita 1.22",
        "deity": "Ritual forces",
        "theme": "Yoking for action",
        "verses": [
          {
            "verse_id": 1,
            "sanskrit": "कस्त्वा युनक्ति स त्वा युनक्ति कस्मै त्वा युनक्ति तस्मै त्वा युनक्ति । कर्मणे वां वेशाय वाम्",
            "transliteration": "kas tvā yunakti sa tvā yunakti kasmai tvā yunakti tasmai tvā yunakti | karmaṇe vāṃ veśāya vām",
            "meaning": "Who yokes you? He yokes you. For whom does he yoke you? For him he yokes you. You two are yoked for action and for its completion."
          }
        ],
        "chant": {
          "type": "Yajus",
          "delivery": "spoken",
          "intonation": "instructional",
          "usage": "Preparation of sacrificial implements"
        }
      },
      {
        "chant_id": "YV-1-23",
        "source_yajurveda": "Vajasaneyi Samhita 1.23",
        "deity": "Agni",
        "theme": "Removal of obstacles",
        "verses": [
          {
            "verse_id": 1,
            "sanskrit": "प्रत्युष्टं रक्षः प्रत्युष्टा अरातयः । निष्टप्तं रक्षो निष्टप्ता अरातयः । उर्वन्तरिक्षमन्वेमि",
            "transliteration": "pratyuṣṭaṃ rakṣaḥ pratyuṣṭā arātayaḥ | niṣṭaptaṃ rakṣo niṣṭaptā arātayaḥ | urv antarikṣam anvemi",
            "meaning": "Scorched are the demons, scorched the hostile powers. Burnt are the demons, burnt the hostile powers. I move through the wide atmosphere."
          }
        ],
        "chant": {
          "type": "Yajus",
          "delivery": "spoken",
          "intonation": "forceful",
          "usage": "Expulsion of negative forces"
        }
      },
      {
        "chant_id": "YV-1-24",
        "source_yajurveda": "Vajasaneyi Samhita 1.24",
        "deity": "Sacrificial yoke",
        "theme": "Protection",
        "verses": [
          {
            "verse_id": 1,
            "sanskrit": "धूरसि धूर्वन्तं धूर्व तं योऽस्मान् धूर्वति तं धूर्व यं वयं धूर्वामः । देवानामसि वह्नितमं सम्नितमं पप्रितमं जुष्टतमं देवहूततमम्",
            "transliteration": "dhūr asi dhūrvantaṃ dhūrva taṃ yo'smān dhūrvati taṃ dhūrva yaṃ vayaṃ dhūrvāmaḥ | devānām asi vahnitamaṃ samnitamaṃ papritamaṃ juṣṭatamam devahūtatamam",
            "meaning": "You are the yoke. Strike down him who would strike us. You are the best bearer of the gods, most united, most filled, most welcomed, best invoker of the gods."
          }
